# Soar does not free the name strings of interned symbols when an agent is
# destroyed (upstream behaviour, in Soar's own pool allocator). The amount is
# fixed per kernel lifetime - about 900 bytes, one string per distinct symbol
# name - and does not grow with decision cycles; the RSS check in
# bridge_test's match simulation guards against growth. Everything allocated
# outside Soar's pool allocator (the bridge, the SML client, the bindings) is
# still checked.
leak:Memory_Manager::allocate_memory
